delete from public.knowledge_chunks where document_id = '75e16704-2d6e-47fc-bf17-489f6ee64a62';

update public.knowledge_documents
set content = $md$Section One: Introduction to the Redemption Policy if Activated
The Company may, at its full administrative discretion, offer an optional service allowing the Alexandria token to be redeemed for assets from the reserve treasury, subject to certain terms, mechanisms, and timeframes to be determined at the relevant time, without this constituting a contractual obligation, a vested right, or a fixed guarantee. The Company reserves the right to suspend, amend, or fully or partially discontinue this service at any time.
This document aims to explain the redemption policy of the Alexandria token as an independent operational policy, established by the Company as a general regulatory framework that may be activated in the future by administrative decision, without this policy currently being active or creating any right or obligation.
The redemption policy is not active at present, and this explanation does not constitute an announcement of redemption opening, a promise to activate it, or a temporal, financial, or contractual obligation toward any party.
This policy is presented for the purposes of: providing advance clarification of the potential mechanism if activation is decided in the future; enhancing regulatory transparency; establishing a non-binding conceptual framework for how the Company may handle redemption if adopted.
The Company expressly confirms that: the redemption policy is not part of the smart contract; it is not part of the whitepaper; it does not constitute a guarantee of token value; it does not grant any current or future right to any token holder to claim redemption. Any potential activation of this policy remains subject solely to an independent administrative decision, made at the sole discretion of the Company, under terms and durations determined at the relevant time.

Section Two: Current Status - Non-Activation of the Redemption Policy
The Company explicitly and conclusively confirms that the redemption policy is not active at present, no redemption window is open, and no redemption requests are received or processed, whether directly or indirectly.
The existence, publication, or explanation of this policy does not give rise to: any current or future right for Alexandria token holders; any obligation on the Company to open redemption; any ability to claim, assert, or interpret an implicit obligation. Any interpretation to the contrary is invalid, non-authoritative, and not binding, regardless of its source, whether from third parties or individual interpretations.
The Company confirms that non-activation of the redemption policy is the current and applicable status, no timeframes are declared or implied, and this policy cannot be relied upon as a legal or financial basis for any claim. Any future redemption, if decided, will remain an exceptional procedure subject to an independent administrative decision and cannot be assumed or inferred merely from the existence of this document.

Section Three: Administrative Decision for Temporary Activation of the Redemption Policy
If the Company decides to activate the redemption policy in the future, such activation shall occur solely through an independent administrative decision for a limited period issued by the Company and subject to its full discretion, without constituting a permanent obligation or commitment to continuity beyond the specified period.
If activated, the duration shall be specifically defined, starting from the official announcement date issued by the Company and ending automatically upon expiration of such period, without any additional notice required.
During the announced activation period: the redemption policy shall not be suspended or terminated before the expiration of the specified period; redemption shall be exercised exclusively under the announced terms. This time-bound commitment shall not be interpreted as a permanent obligation, a vested right, or a token value guarantee.
The Company expressly confirms that: the expiration of the period automatically terminates the redemption policy; no obligation to renew arises upon expiration; compliance during the period does not constitute a precedent or commitment to future activations. The scope of redemption, during the activation period, remains subject to the operational and regulatory conditions determined by the Company, without changing the legal nature of the token or converting it into an investment instrument or a claim-right.

Section Four: Relationship Between the Redemption Policy, the Reserve, and the Token's Cumulative Effect
The Alexandria token is linked to a reserve system that operates on the principle of relative weighted correlation, where the reserve is considered a structural element supporting the long-term sustainability of the system. It is not a market pricing mechanism, nor a direct commitment to redemption or value repayment.
This design produces what is known as the cumulative effect of the token, whereby the token's weighted value automatically increases as the reserve expands, without requiring any activity from the token holder, any trading or speculation, or any direct operational intervention. This cumulative effect is a structural property within the system, entirely independent of the redemption policy, whether the policy is inactive or active.
The Company expressly confirms that the reserve treasury within the Alexandria system does not constitute a reference price for the token, nor does it constitute a redemption guarantee or obligation to repay value. Growth of the reserve does not create any automatic duty to open or activate the redemption mechanism.
Within this framework, the reserve represents a general structural reserve linked to the total token supply of 100,000,000 tokens and is considered allocated to the entire issued token quantity without exception, regardless of any specific category, whether circulating or non-circulating. The reserve is neither divisible, allocated, nor redistributed based on redemption, trading, or individual holdings.
This comprehensive linkage is used exclusively for the structural weighted measurement of the system as a whole and shall not be interpreted under any circumstances as a basis for creating individual rights, financial obligations, or claimable entitlements.
If the Company decides to activate the redemption policy in the future, such policy will operate as a separate and independent operational mechanism, applied for a specific timeframe under its own conditions, and shall not be interpreted as converting the cumulative effect into a direct or claimable financial right, nor shall it create any legal or contractual overlap between the structural reserve and the redemption policy.
Thus, the cumulative effect remains a structural property within the Alexandria system, while the redemption policy remains a temporary administrative option subject solely to the Company's discretion, without any direct or indirect legal or financial obligation.

Section Five: Operational Redemption Mechanism Upon Activation Only
If the redemption policy is activated by administrative decision as described in the previous sections, the redemption mechanism shall be applied exclusively during the specified activation period and in accordance with the operational and regulatory conditions adopted by the Company at that time. Redemption is subject to the following conditions:

1. Official Submission: no redemption request shall be accepted except through the official channels specified by the Company, and in accordance with approved forms and procedures.

2. Verification and Compliance: redemption applicants are subject to mandatory verification procedures, including identity verification (KYC), compliance and anti-money laundering (AML) requirements, and any additional documents requested by the Company. Failure to complete these requirements is sufficient grounds for rejecting the request.

3. No Maximum Limit: the Company does not establish a fixed maximum for the number of tokens redeemable during the activation period, but a minimum threshold representing the weight of one gram must be met. However, for large redemption quantities, the requesting party must notify the Company in advance within a timeframe determined by the Company for organizational, operational, and logistical reasons. Failure to provide prior notice is a valid reason to delay or not process the request within the specified period.

4. Personal Attendance or Approved Mechanism: redemption shall be carried out through the mechanism adopted by the Company, whether by personal attendance at a designated location or via an approved operational method, without constituting an obligation to adopt a specific method.

5. Priority of Requests: redemption requests shall be processed according to a chronological or organizational order determined by the Company, without any guarantee that all requests will be processed before the end of the activation period.

6. Right of Acceptance or Rejection: the Company reserves full discretion to accept or reject any redemption request, delay requests for operational or organizational reasons, or reject requests for non-compliance with procedures, without this giving rise to any claim or compensation rights.

Illustrative calculation example (weighted share per token = total reserve weight / total number of tokens; total number of tokens = 100,000,000):
- Reserve of 100 grams (100,000 milligrams): 100,000 / 100,000,000 = 0.001 mg per token. Each Alexandria token represents 0.001 mg of the reserve, i.e. 1000 Alexandria tokens = 1 mg.
- Reserve of 500 grams (500,000 milligrams): 500,000 / 100,000,000 = 0.005 mg per token. Each Alexandria token represents 0.005 mg of the reserve, i.e. 200 Alexandria tokens = 1 mg.
- Reserve of 1,000 grams / 1 kg (1,000,000 milligrams): 1,000,000 / 100,000,000 = 0.01 mg per token. Each Alexandria token represents 0.01 mg of the reserve, i.e. 100 Alexandria tokens = 1 mg.
- Reserve of 2,000 grams / 2 kg (2,000,000 milligrams): 2,000,000 / 100,000,000 = 0.02 mg per token. Each Alexandria token represents 0.02 mg of the reserve, i.e. 50 Alexandria tokens = 1 mg.

This allocation is used exclusively for theoretical calculation purposes and does not create any redemption right, individual value, or legal or financial obligation, and cannot be relied upon as a basis for any claim. These examples are for illustration purposes only. The actual weighted value shall be calculated exclusively at the time of submitting a redemption request and during the service window, in accordance with the operational conditions and administrative decisions in effect at that time.

Section Six: Fees and Costs Associated with the Redemption Process
If the redemption policy is activated, the redemption process shall be subject to a fixed operational fee of 2.5% of the redemption transaction value, calculated exclusively for operational and regulatory purposes. This percentage includes, without limitation: administrative and operational costs; verification and compliance costs (KYC/AML); storage and custody costs; gold insurance costs; transportation and execution costs; legal and regulatory costs associated with the process.
The Company expressly confirms that the 2.5% fee does not constitute a deduction from the token's weighted value, does not affect the cumulative effect linked to the reserve, and does not represent an exchange rate or trading commission.
This fee applies only at the execution of the redemption transaction, exclusively during the announced activation period.
The Company further confirms that payment of the fee does not create any vested right to complete the redemption, does not guarantee the token holder that the request will be accepted, and does not give rise to any claim or compensation in the event of request rejection or postponement.
The Company reserves the right to adjust the fee percentage for any future activation and to apply different fees during other activation periods, without this being considered an obligation or precedent.

Section Seven: Non-Binding Nature and Disclaimer
The Company expressly acknowledges and confirms that the redemption policy, whether inactive or active for a specific period, does not, under any circumstances, create a permanent legal or financial obligation, nor grant any Alexandria token holder a vested or claimable right.
This policy, or any part of it, shall not be interpreted as a guarantee of token value, a commitment to repurchase tokens, an obligation to repay funds or assets, or a conversion of the token into an investment instrument, debt instrument, or claim-right.
The Company further confirms that any activation of the redemption policy is conducted within a temporary administrative and operational framework, does not create a contractual relationship between the Company and token holders, and does not limit the Company's authority to manage the system or the reserve.
The Company fully disclaims liability for any direct or indirect losses, any price expectations or financial conclusions, and any decisions made by token holders based on this policy or their interpretation of it. Each token holder bears full individual responsibility for their decisions and acknowledges that owning tokens does not grant any legal right to claim redemption, whether during or outside the activation period, except within the procedural limits determined by the Company for the specified timeframe.

Section Eight: Final Authority and Right to Amend or Cancel
The Company retains full and final authority to interpret, apply, and manage the redemption policy and all related matters. Any decision issued by the Company in this regard is administratively binding within the system and does not create a legal or contractual obligation toward any party.
The Company has the absolute discretion, at any time, to amend this policy in whole or in part, update its terms or procedures, cancel or replace it with another policy, or withdraw it entirely from circulation or publication, without the need to provide reasons, and without incurring any legal, financial, or compensatory liability.
The Company also confirms that any previous version of this policy is not considered a binding reference; only the latest officially approved and published version by the Company is authoritative; copies that are saved, transferred, or outdated cannot be relied upon.
Any amendment, cancellation, or update does not affect the legal nature of the token, the Company's rights to manage the reserve and the system, or any other regulatory policies or documents issued by the Company. This policy constitutes an independent regulatory document, subject to updates and amendments as the Company deems appropriate for the benefit and sustainability of the system.

Source: https://www.alexandriaecosystem.com/en/redemption-policy$md$,
